# Build context exclusions.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE THE IMAGE SHIPPED EVERY LIVE CREDENTIAL. `COPY . .` copies
# the build context, and the build context is NOT filtered by .gitignore — so
# backend/.env, which is correctly gitignored and has never been committed, was
# nonetheless baked into every image at /app/.env: GROQ_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY,
# NVIDIA_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY, INDIANAPI_KEY, ADMIN_API_KEY, the
# DATABASE_URL with its password, and — worst of the set — JWT_SECRET_KEY
# (forge any user's session) and TOTP_ENCRYPTION_KEY (decrypt every user's 2FA
# secret at rest). Anyone who could pull, export or exec the image had all of
# them, and `docker history` would keep them even after a later delete.
#
# It also copied the local venv/ — 1.3 GB of Python 3.10 packages into a
# Python 3.12 image, which is both a 4.19 GB -> ~700 MB size difference and a
# second, mismatched interpreter's dependency tree sitting next to the real one.
#
# Runtime configuration comes from the environment (Render/k8s/compose all
# inject it), never from a file in the image.

# ── Secrets: nothing resembling real configuration enters the image ──────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ── Local virtualenvs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
venv/
.venv/
env/
ENV/

# ── Python build artefacts ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/

# ── Test and tooling artefacts (not needed at runtime) ───────────────────────
tests/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
pytest.ini

# ── VCS / editor / OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
.DS_Store

# ── Local logs and scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
